            "organization": "NASA Langley Research Center"
          }
        ],
        "date": "2013-01-03",
        "description": "The original version of this model, dated 2012-08-09, was a simple mixer that took pilot controls and converted them into control surface deflections directly. This version includes an LQR-designed longitudinal and lateral-directional stabilization system as well as logic to follow altitude, airspeed, and ground track angle. Lateral offset from course feedback can be provided to improve performance or zero can be provided for just a heading command feature.",
        "modification_id": "A"
      },
